  "answer": "No retiming of the lead car was shown to make VaVAM rear-end it at 2 Hz planning, and none of the requested cases was confirmed (the goal was not met). The only setting that produced any failures was 096988dd at -0.5 s, 1.0x (S5), and its 90% range reaches both below and above 0.5, so it is not confirmed as a mostly-failing case. Those failures were also not rear-ends: in each one the policy drifted left into vehicle 41 in the next lane while the lead truck stayed well ahead. Every other setting was clean, but most had only one or two runs. That is a hint that these settings pass, not a measured rate, and the ranges still allow sizeable failure rates.",
